      "message": "Why was this changed to do a .get_user first? If this is to guard the callback against errors, in theory the callback should be smart enough / handle the exception. I would rather not see the driver interface changed.\n\nNotifications are sent after the action is taken in either case, and if the user doesn\u0027t exist there will be an exception before you get into the notification event callback",
